## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **First variant-select approach (Bug A "fix")** — nulled `drive_web_view_url` to fix browser cache, but that (plus leaving canonical `filename` = `-v01-APPROVED.png` with no such file on disk + null Drive) made the ref BYTE-UNREACHABLE for the server reader. VGEN preflights the WHOLE episode's refs, so 3 dead refs blocked ALL 23 Video Artists ("Media unreachable"). Root cause: `readAssetMediaAsBase64` resolves ONLY by canonical `filename` (cache→Drive→/staging/), never a `/api/media/…` staging URL. Fixed in 637f6c3 (copy attempt bytes → canonical filename; keep attempt's drive_file_id).
- **MCP `execute_sql` (Supabase)** — denied ("no permission"). Use node-inline from `webapp/` with service role instead.
- **node-inline DB scripts from repo root** — fail (`@supabase/supabase-js` not resolvable). MUST `cd /c/SandyStudio/webapp` first. Also: backslash Windows paths get mangled in bash heredocs — use forward slashes.
- **budget_log `.select('metadata')`** — column doesn't exist; select only cost_usd/created_at/agent_id.

